---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — WorthIt"
  description="Terms for using WorthIt on iPhone to check shelf prices, resale, grocery lists, and receipts."
>
  <main class="legal-page" id="main">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">WORTHIT</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">
        Effective date: May 10, 2026 · <a href="/">WorthIt home</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      </p>
      <div class="legal-shell">
        <p>
          These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your use of the WorthIt mobile application and related services (the
          “Service”), operated by an independent developer. A formal legal entity name will be added here when
          incorporated. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
        </p>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about these Terms, email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
        <h2>The Service</h2>
        <p>
          WorthIt provides product-related insights using images, barcodes, and text you submit, including shelf-price
          checks (Save), resale estimates (Flip), grocery list compare, and receipt logging. Results are informational
          estimates, not professional, financial, or legal advice. You are responsible for your purchasing and selling
          decisions.
        </p>
        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          You agree not to misuse the Service, probe systems you do not own, or attempt to circumvent technical limits
          (including analysis quotas enforced on our servers).
        </p>
        <h2>Third-party retailers</h2>
        <p>
          The app may open third-party retailers (for example Amazon, Walmart, or Target) in your device browser. Those
          sites set their own prices, terms, and privacy practices; we do not control them.
        </p>
        <h2>Amazon Associates</h2>
        <p>
          WorthIt is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program
          designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com and
          related sites. If you use links that include our Amazon associate tag, we may earn commissions from qualifying
          purchases. Amazon and related marks are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.
        </p>
        <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
        <p>
          WorthIt Pro and other paid plans, when offered, are billed through the Apple App Store (or Google Play when
          available). Payment, renewal, cancellation, and refunds follow the store’s terms. Subscription management is
          available through your device account settings and in-app subscription tools.
        </p>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms; continued use after changes means you accept the updated Terms where allowed by law.
          This page is published at https://isitworthit.io/terms.
        </p>
        <p>These Terms are not a substitute for advice from a lawyer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
